# The unit-file, fstab and manager lines PID 1 may make, link or mount a host path for (#5167): in every
# file under the unit directories (and each link's target), each [Mount] line whole, and each other line
# whose value holds a '/' or that sets one of StateDirectory=, RuntimeDirectory=, CacheDirectory=,
# LogsDirectory= or ConfigurationDirectory=, at a setting mkosi.finalize does not list as one PID 1 only
# reads or that only names units, users or numbers (PID1_READS, PID1_NAMES, Condition*, Assert*, Exec*);
# every etc/fstab line but comments; and every system.conf and system.conf.d line (ManagerEnvironment= is
# refused outright). A unit's name alone (a lineless .automount) is held by the unit-made directory rules. One per line: the file's path in the image
# tree, a tab, and "[Section] Key=value" (fstab: the line). mkosi.finalize fails the build on any such
# line not here, exactly and under its own file; its other unit rules still weigh every line here.
# A driver drivers.json lists needs no entry: its units are DRIVER_TEMPLATE's, reviewed in mkosi.finalize.
# Review a new line for what PID 1 makes, links or mounts for it: a bind, an overlay or a subdirectory
# mount gives a path a second name, so a mount line is listed only if it names no host path as its
# source. The failed build prints each new line as "entry: <file><TAB><value>". With the image tree:
#   python3 image/mkosi/mkosi.finalize --made-allowlist ROOT > image/mkosi/made.allow
etc/fstab	devtmpfs /dev     devtmpfs nosuid,noexec       0 0
etc/fstab	tmpfs    /dev/shm tmpfs    nosuid,nodev,noexec 0 0
etc/fstab	tmpfs    /run     tmpfs    mode=0755,nosuid,nodev,noexec 0 0
